Z||000000||Jncomutt||07-22-2001||09:28 PM||||Since I've had my car the idle has always been a 'lil screwy.  When I first start it, the idle likes to stay up around 2k - 2500 for about 2-3 mins and is very steady and smooth, but then it will come down to about 1000 and be rough.  The car will idle ok for a few seconds then make a low sort of pop noise and the idle will stumble to about 800 and catch itself, come up to about 1100 then stay at 1000, make that low pop, stumble..etc...   You get the idea.  Well recently I've noticed that if I'm just cruising at about 45 in 4th gear (4spd) You can very very slightly feel the car surge.  It doesn't reflect it in the RPM or in the speed, but theres a definate feeling.  I've checked a few of the vacume lines and was able to find no leak.  (Does anyone know if they sell replacement steel ones like Dickmans for the 4 cyl?)<P>Also I've recently replaced my plugs to AC Delco Rapidfires, added a MSD BLASTER GM coil, And a MSD 6A ignition and noticed that my gas mileage actually dropped.  I used to notice that my 4cyl would get about 150mi to a half tank, now it only reaches about 120mi.  The gauge is reading accurate, because it will take 8.5 gallons when it just gets to the red like it always has.<P>As always, any help will be appreciated... TIA<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||HummelHund||07-22-2001||10:32 PM||||Are you getting any codes? My car is having a similar problem, so far I've replaced all the vacuum hoses, the MAP sensor, the IAC, the TPS, and put new plugs, wires, dist. cap and rotor on it. I still haven't totally fixed it. EGR maybe? I'd narrow down the cheap stuff first. Do a search for idle problems and it may give you some more help.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
